/// MATERIALISE-BEFORE form: the inline arms BOTH call `materialize_flags(&mut
/// flags_reg, &mut lazy)` as the FIRST statement (`lib.rs:29313` / `29656`),
/// unconditionally, before ANY divergence.  The shim therefore materialises
/// first (the landed `op_bcd` discipline) and passes the materialised flags;
/// this fn never re-materialises (neither inline arm does after the leading
/// `materialize_flags`). Watched returns, returns to an outer ring and faults
/// are terminal; an unwatched same-ring success restarts the outer decode
/// loop after CS changes.
///
/// The whole arm body (cross-privilege SS:ESP/SS:SP pop, `load_cs_iret`,
/// `retf_nullify_segments`, null-CS sentinel, `dpmi_retf_cleanup`,
/// `mark_retf`/`ret_guard_pop`) is moved VERBATIM.  Every inline
/// `cpu.regs.flags = flags_reg; return RunResult::X` becomes `out.flags =
/// flags_reg; out.lazy = LazyOp::None; return ArmFlow::Return(RunResult::X)` —
/// the shim's `cpu.regs.flags = out.flags` is the byte-identical redundant
/// write (the run_ext terminal-return invariant).  `ram` rebinds via
/// `mem.core().ram_base_ptr()` exactly as inline and travels back via `out.ram`.
/// `executed` is the PRE-increment value on every fault return and `+1` only
/// on the success return, exactly as inline.  `0xCA` consumes `imm16`
/// (`pos += 2`) verbatim; the arm always `Return`s so `pos` is irrelevant
